---
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <meta name="description" content='Who is "everyone"? Analyzing media practices of (national) belonging — an international workshop, November 12–13, 2026, University of Applied Arts Vienna.' />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500&family=Source+Serif+4:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
    <title>Who is "everyone"? — Workshop</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="border-b border-[color:var(--color-rule)]">
      <nav class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 md:px-10 h-16 flex items-center">
        <a href="/" class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)] hover:text-[color:var(--color-ink)] transition-colors">
          ← Back to project
        </a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 md:px-10 py-24 md:py-32">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-accent)] mb-6">International Workshop · November 12–13, 2026</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl leading-[1.1] tracking-tight max-w-4xl">
        Who is "everyone"?<br/>
        <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Analyzing media practices of (national) belonging</span>
      </h1>

      <dl class="mt-12 grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-sm border-t border-b border-[color:var(--color-rule)] py-8">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-muted)] mb-2">Date</dt>
          <dd>November 12–13, 2026<br/>Thu 9:00–18:00 · Fri 9:30–16:30</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-muted)] mb-2">Venue</dt>
          <dd>Universität für angewandte Kunst Wien<br/>Vordere Zollamtsstraße 7, 1030 Vienna · Flux 2</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-muted)] mb-2">Convened by</dt>
          <dd>Birgit Haberpeuntner<br/>Primarily English · two talks in German (★)</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <div class="mt-12 max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.8] text-[color:var(--color-ink)]/85">
        <p>
          Modern mass media address everyone and each individual at once. Taking Brecht's question
          of who counts as "everyone" as its starting point, this workshop examines how media practices
          produce, negotiate, and delimit belonging. At its center stands nationhood, which continues
          to function as a powerful category of social organization and collective subjectivation, even
          though its disappearance in globalized media environments has been proclaimed for decades.
          At the same time, the workshop asks about emergent or alternative forms of collectivization
          beyond national framings. Scholars from media culture studies, communication studies,
          sociology, history, film studies, and musicology bring their methods into dialogue.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3">
        <a href="/downloads/who-is-everyone-program-abstracts.pdf" target="_blank" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-[color:var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/><polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"/><line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3"/></svg>
          Download Program &amp; Abstracts (PDF)
        </a>
        <a href="/workshop-everyone-cfp" class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)] hover:text-[color:var(--color-ink)] transition-colors">
          Read the original Call for Papers →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- DAY 1 -->
      <div class="mt-16 border-t border-[color:var(--color-rule)] pt-12">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-accent)] mb-8">Day 1 — Thursday, November 12</p>

        <div class="space-y-10">
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">08:45–09:00</span>
            <span class="md:col-span-10">Registration &amp; Welcome</span>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">09:00–09:30</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <span class="font-medium">Introduction &amp; Framing</span>
              <p class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)] mt-1">"Who is 'everyone'?" – Questions, Concept, Aims</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">09:30–11:30</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Panel 1 · Chaired by Sabina Mihelj</p>
              <p class="font-medium mb-3">Everyday &amp; Digital Practices of National Belonging</p>
              <ul class="space-y-2 text-[color:var(--color-ink)]/80">
                <li>(K)Einheit verhandeln? The (de)construction of German unity — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Annika Werner</span></li>
                <li>"That's exactly how we do it, too": Digital-ethnographic approaches to the performance of community — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Jana Stöxen</span></li>
                <li>Who Counts as "Us"? DeepSeek, AI Nationalism, and National Belonging in China — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Dechun Zhang &amp; Yuxi Huang</span></li>
                <li>Indian Elections in the gaze of Google — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Vihang Jumle</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">11:30–11:45</span>
            <span class="md:col-span-10 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] italic">Coffee Break</span>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">11:45–13:15</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Panel 2 · Chaired by Birgit Haberpeuntner</p>
              <p class="font-medium mb-3">Archives, Infrastructures, Networks</p>
              <ul class="space-y-2 text-[color:var(--color-ink)]/80">
                <li>Paratactics Against "Methodological Nationalism" — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Philip Widmann</span></li>
                <li>Internationality through Categorization: Media Practices of Belonging in <em>Infermental</em> (1982–1991) — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">András Keskeny</span> ★</li>
                <li>From 'all' to 'us': Alternative News Agencies and the Shift in Global Narratives — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Leonie Wolters</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">13:15–14:30</span>
            <span class="md:col-span-10 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] italic">Lunch</span>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">14:30–16:00</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Panel 3 · Chaired by Stefan Benedik</p>
              <p class="font-medium mb-3">Imaging Unity: Gender, Authoritarian Visual Orders, and Their Afterlives</p>
              <ul class="space-y-2 text-[color:var(--color-ink)]/80">
                <li>The Iconization of a 'We': National Public Sphere and the Female Body as an Image of Pseudo-Unity — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Sahar Daryab</span> ★</li>
                <li>Staged Belonging: Heimat, Gender, and National Community in Austrofascist Media Policy — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Christina Wieder</span></li>
                <li>All'armi, siam fascisti – The Question of Community in Antifascist Italian Film — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Naemi Haar</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">16:00–16:15</span>
            <span class="md:col-span-10 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] italic">Coffee Break</span>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">16:15–17:15</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <p class="font-medium">Method Café</p>
              <p class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)] mt-1">Three small groups, mixed across panels, work through guiding questions. Brief summaries by the group hosts.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">17:15–18:00</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <p class="font-medium">Day 1 Response</p>
              <p class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)] mt-1">Sabina Mihelj and Michael Skey follow up on all three panels and the Method Café in a synthesizing response before the room opens up.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">from 19:00</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <p class="font-medium">Guided Tour: House of Austrian History (hdgö)</p>
              <p class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)] mt-1">By Stefan Benedik, Head of Public History and Deputy Director. Please register!</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- DAY 2 -->
      <div class="mt-16 border-t border-[color:var(--color-rule)] pt-12">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-accent)] mb-8">Day 2 — Friday, November 13</p>

        <div class="space-y-10">
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">09:30–11:00</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Panel 4 · Chaired by Elias Berner</p>
              <p class="font-medium mb-3">Felt Belonging: Frontal Images, Pop Music, and Ancient Landscapes</p>
              <ul class="space-y-2 text-[color:var(--color-ink)]/80">
                <li>All in the Face: Frontality, Belonging and the Control Image — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Sebastian Lederle</span></li>
                <li>Russia's Pop Music Propaganda Since the Beginning of the War in Ukraine — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Johann Pibert</span></li>
                <li>Driving the ancient landscape: Encountering the homeland's roots in West Germany and the UK (1950–1975) — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Hilbrand Wouters</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">11:00–11:30</span>
            <span class="md:col-span-10 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] italic">Coffee Break</span>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">11:30–13:00</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Panel 5 · Chaired by Michael Skey</p>
              <p class="font-medium mb-3">Nationhood in Emergent Media: Generated, Played, Lived</p>
              <ul class="space-y-2 text-[color:var(--color-ink)]/80">
                <li>Life in Platform Nations: Exploring Citizen Engagement with Digital Sovereignty — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">César Jiménez-Martínez (with Sabina Mihelj)</span></li>
                <li>Hallucinating the nation: A comparative multi-modal analysis of genAI's visual regimes of representation — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Delia Dumitrica (with Maria Avraamidou)</span></li>
                <li>Gaming the Nation: Video Games as Possibility Spaces for National Identity Formation — <span class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">Rachel van der Merwe</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">13:00–14:30</span>
            <span class="md:col-span-10 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] italic">Lunch</span>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">14:30–15:30</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <p class="font-medium">Blind Spot: Nation?</p>
              <p class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)] mt-1">Sabina Mihelj, Michael Skey, Maja Figge &amp; Leonie Kapfer in conversation. Short position statements on the role of "nation" as an analytic category, then open debate.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">15:30–16:00</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <p class="font-medium">Who is 'everyone'? Revisited</p>
              <p class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)] mt-1">Open closing discussion, informed by two days of case studies.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-2 md:gap-8 text-sm">
            <span class="md:col-span-2 text-[color:var(--color-muted)] tabular-nums">16:00–16:30</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-10">
              <p class="font-medium">Wrap-Up, Publication Opportunity, Next Steps</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 border-t border-[color:var(--color-rule)] pt-8">
        <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)] mb-1">★ Talk given in German; English slides and an English abstract are provided.</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)] mt-6 italic">
          This workshop is part of the research project <em>The Remediation of Nation</em> and is
          funded by the Austrian Academy of Sciences (OeAW) through its APART-GSK programme.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 md:px-10 py-8 border-t border-[color:var(--color-rule)] text-xs text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
      <span>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Birgit Haberpeuntner</span>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
